WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.120
- We always close out the
show with one last story,

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:04.310
to lift your spirits
and brighten your day,

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:06.610
and all February in honor
of black history month,

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:08.570
we are shining a light
on African-Americans

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:11.600
bringing joy, enrichment
and compassion to the world.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:12.800
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:17.470
So I want to tell y'all about a former

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:21.260
college football player turned
psychology PhD candidate,

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:22.980
who's getting kids excited to go to

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:25.650
historically black
colleges and universities.

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:29.450
It's all through his new
book, H is for HBCUs.

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:32.040
Not only does the book
help kids learn to read

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:35.530
it also teaches them how
HBCUs have helped mold

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:38.100
Some of the nation's most
renowned change makers.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.850
I'm talking about greats
like Kamala Harris,

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:43.370
Oprah Winfrey, and
Martin Luther king, Jr..

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:44.480
My gosh.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.160
We have the author on the line right now,

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:48.090
dialing in from Nashville where he watches

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:49.570
on news channel five.

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:50.423
Hi Henry.

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:53.920
- How did you come up with
the idea for the book?

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.960
- Yes, so my siblings went to HBCUs

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:59.070
and I didn't cause I
went and played football

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:01.220
at a PWI full scholarship.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:02.520
So I was there when there were a lot

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:04.040
of racial injustice and you know,

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:05.970
just a lot of different plights that

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:07.410
we were going through as black people

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:08.540
that I didn't feel comfortable

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:09.980
were seen or have a voice.

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:12.500
So a lot of my times my
siblings would talk about

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:13.860
how they felt seen and heard and

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:15.260
that community they had,

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:18.290
so when I decided to go
to HBC for grad school,

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:19.980
Tennessee State was the perfect fit.

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:21.940
I met great mentors.

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:24.490
I met, you know, people of
color that looked like me,

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:26.730
that thought like me,
that we could collab with.

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:28.730
And I really felt that same sense of love

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:30.410
and that mentorship I received.

00:01:30.410 --> 00:01:32.510
So I wanted to start that at an early age

00:01:32.510 --> 00:01:34.390
for young children starting
at pre-K, kindergarten

00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:36.200
to get that exposure and hopefully

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:38.680
they'll choose the HBCU
when it comes that time.

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:39.513
- Oh, that's amazing.

00:01:39.513 --> 00:01:42.070
So can you tell us more,
I love that picture.

00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:44.020
Can you tell us more
about what's in the book?

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:46.310
- Yeah, so the book is from A to Z,

00:01:46.310 --> 00:01:48.430
each letter is connected to an

00:01:48.430 --> 00:01:50.221
historically black college or university

00:01:50.221 --> 00:01:52.240
or prominent African-American
that went there.

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:54.416
So we've got people like Lonnie Johnson,

00:01:54.416 --> 00:01:55.280
the inventor of the Super Soaker

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:56.710
who some black kids didn't know

00:01:56.710 --> 00:01:57.650
he invented the Super Soaker.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:00.270
We've also got a gospel
legend Yolanda Adams

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:02.370
who went to Texas Southern.

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:05.330
So, and Kamala Harris,
we've got people like

00:02:05.330 --> 00:02:06.163
Langston Hughes.

00:02:06.163 --> 00:02:07.347
- Wow.

00:02:07.347 --> 00:02:08.450
- We've got just all
sorts of different people.

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:11.330
We got sport athletes, we have
politicians, we have poets.

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:13.070
So just a lot of people that, you know,

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:14.660
just gives you a glimpse
and a little inkling

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:15.810
of who these people are,

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:17.370
why they're important and just hopefully

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:20.082
gain hat knowledge for HBCUs

00:02:20.082 --> 00:02:21.050
and the people that went there.

00:02:21.050 --> 00:02:22.570
- And also that confidence for,

00:02:22.570 --> 00:02:24.120
for kids to see people that look like them

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:26.320
doing amazing things and that
they can accomplish that.

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:28.510
It's all around just a really great book

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:30.070
for any child, really.

00:02:30.070 --> 00:02:31.350
Thank you so much, Henry.

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:32.790
Coming from a mom of two young kids,

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:34.600
I can not wait to read it with my kids.

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:37.320
I'm liking your post right now

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:38.410
and that's not all, my man.

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:41.120
Our season long partner,
Pilot Pen, makers of G2,

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:42.750
the go-to pen of the Kelly Clarkson show,

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:45.550
want to honor ultimate
overachievers just like you.

00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:46.700
So they're gonna be writing you a check

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:49.000
for a thousand dollars
just 'cause you're rad.

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:52.490
- Oh wow.

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:53.730
I appreciate that so much.

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:54.563
Thank you.

00:02:54.563 --> 00:02:56.453
- Absolutely, thank you so much Henry.

